
To clone private GitHub repositories using SSH
----------------------------------------------
1. Generate ssh key
 ssh-keygen -t rsa -b 4096 -C "youremail@gmail.com.com"

2.to start ssh agent
eval "$(ssh-agent -s)"

you see the output: Agent pid 12345

3.Add the SSH Key to the Agent
ssh-add C:/Users/QSP-Corp2/.ssh/id_rsa

4.Add SSH Key to GitHub
cat ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub

-Go to your GitHub account:
-Navigate to Settings → SSH and GPG Keys.
-Click New SSH Key.
-In the Title field, enter a name for this key (e.g., "Windows PC").
-Paste your SSH public key into the Key field.
-Click Add SSH Key.

5.Test the SSH Connection
ssh -T git@github.com

On success, you'll see this message: Hi username! You've successfully authenticated, but GitHub does not provide shell access.

6.Test by cloning the repository
git clone git@github.com:username/repo-name.git
  
